    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Description\n\n_**NOTE:** This can be a one-time occurrence or not, so I would not put it in high priority._\r\n\r\nSome completion items have the type `MiniCompletion:signature-help`\r\n\r\nI do not know how this actually happens. And for now, it only happens in one of my Files.\r\nWhat I can currently see, when this happens:\r\n\r\n* Signature Help (also correctly highlighted)\r\n* Completion list with the keyword and only those two have the wrong type\r\n\r\nI will update this ticket if it occurs multiple times and consistently.\r\nMaybe you have an idea, how this could happen. \r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/677821/fb6d286b-9854-4c7f-92a0-626ce78a816d)\r\n\r\nConfig\r\n```lua\r\n-- Plugin: mini.completion\r\nMiniCompletion.setup({\r\n  window = {\r\n    info = {\r\n      border = 'single',\r\n    },\r\n    signature = {\r\n      border = 'single',\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.5\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nI do not know how to reproduce\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n_No response_\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nInternal buffer name is used as type.",
