            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nThis is how default fallback completion (via `<C-n>`) works: it shows as \"kind\" the buffer name. The steps to reproduce this is to type a word which triggers fallback completion and is present in signature help. Example for empty Lua file: `string.find(` followed by `patt`.\r\n\r\nClosing as not an issue per se.",
